# Underrealm Lich: "Underrealm Lich's first ability applies even if you have fewer than three cards in your library. If you
# have no cards in your library, you can't lose the game for trying to draw a card from an empty library" (its ruling;
# CR 121.6a, 609.3). Bot1's library holds two cards as Ancestral Recall resolves: the first draw looks at those two, Bot1
# takes the Forest and the other goes to its graveyard; the second and third draws look at nothing. Its turn 3 draw for the
# turn is replaced too, and Bot1 is still in the game afterwards, having never drawn from its empty library.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Underrealm Lich
Ancestral Recall
Plains
Forest
Mountain

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Underrealm Lich.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Arrange(Forest | Mountain)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Result = InProgress
Bot1.LostTo = (absent)
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Forest
Bot1.Library.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Mountain; Black Lotus
